hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"333","Ali bin Hajar Al-Saadi told us, Ismail told us, meaning Ibn Jafar, Al-Alaa bin Abdul Rahman bin Yaqoub told us, that he entered upon Anas Ibn Malik was in his house in Basra, until he finished the noon prayer. He said: His house was next to the mosque. When we entered it, he said: Did you pray the afternoon prayer? We said to him: We had just finished the noon hour. He said: They prayed the afternoon prayer, so we stood up and prayed. When we departed, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. God, upon him be peace, says: “That is the prayer of the hypocrite. He sits and watches the sun, until when it is between the horns of Satan, he stands up and pecks it four times, without mentioning “Allah is therein except a little.” On the authority of Yunus bin Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Ibn Wahb, that Malik narrated to him, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of this."
"334","We are Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Bazi`, we are Abdul Rahman bin Othman al-Bakrawi Abu Bahr, we are Shu`bah, we are Al-Ala bin Abdul Rahman. Ibn Yaqub means, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said. He said: And I heard Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna say: I found in my book, in my own handwriting, in what I copied from the book, Ibn Ja’far, he said: Na Shu’bah, He said: I heard Al-Alaa bin Abdul-Rahman narrating, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “This is a prayer The hypocrite waits until when the sun turns yellow and it is between the horns of Satan, or on the horns of Satan, and he rises and pecks it four times. He does not remember God. Therein except a little.” This is the wording of the hadith of Abu Musa, and Ibn Bazi’ said: “Between the horns of Satan or within the horns of Satan,” and he said: Shu’bah said: “He pecked it four times without mentioning it.” God is therein except a little.”"
